Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-29-2001||04:15 PM||||Which size speaker is best for me to put in my dash?  an in the rear area(4x6 spot) which should I put 4, or 4x6?<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW2b.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||kempo||11-29-2001||04:23 PM||||If it were me, I'd put in JL speakers if you can find them.  My second choice would be Kenwood excelon 4x6's.  If money is no option, go with a really good quality speaker.  <BR>It really depends on what you want.  If you want squeeky clean high range speakers or something that'll give you some bass.  If you get back on that, I can recommend some to you.  <P>Edit-<BR>As for your dash, 4x10's are the worst kind of speaker imagineable.  I use mine for highs, so I built a custom plate and use 3.5" MB Quart speakers up there.  They sound incredible.  No matter what you decide, stay as far away from 4x10's as you can.<p>[This message has been edited by kempo (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||11-29-2001||04:26 PM||||The smaller the speaker...the less bass you get.<P>You want midbass up front...4x10 or larger.<P>Rears can be anything.  I have 4" components.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-29-2001||06:21 PM||||I have 4" component speakers in all for corners. They are Polk Audio EX series II.<BR>They sound GREAT. Using a seperate 8" sub woofer for the lows.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
